  <data name="Tutorial_WelcomeText" xml:space="preserve"><value>KackZug checks your train connections to work and speaks up loudly when something's off.</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_UpdatedText" xml:space="preserve"><value>KackZug was updated to version {0}. Here's a quick recap of what matters.</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_ShareTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Share a connection</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_ShareText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Look up your connection to work in DB Navigator, tap “Share” and pick KackZug. Then save it as the outbound or return trip of a shift, for example “Early shift”.</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_WeekTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Plan your week</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_WeekText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Under “Week” you give each day a shift or leave it free. You can switch off the outbound and return trip per day. A new week can copy last week's plan if you like.</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_CheckTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check and alert</value></data>
  <data name="Tutorial_CheckText" xml:space="preserve"><value>KackZug checks the evening before and shortly before departure. If a train is cancelled or late, changes platform or a connection gets tight, a loud alarm goes off.</value></data>
